kosha chlorine

  -- Cl. proton-17. period 3, group 17 halogen. valence: 7 (gains 1 electron).
  -- yellow-green gas at room temperature. toxic. bleaching agent.
  -- Cl⁻ (chloride ion): essential in biology — HCl in stomach acid, nerve signals.
  -- NaCl: ionic bond with sodium — table salt, most common ionic compound.
  -- disinfectant in water treatment. PVC polymer backbone.
  -- covalent: Cl2 gas; ionic: NaCl, KCl; organic: chloroform, DDT.

